Stochastic differential equations (SDEs) extend the deterministic trajectories from ODEs with stochastic trajectories. A stochastic trajectory is commonly called a stochastic process (Xt)0≤t≤1 and is given by
Xt is a random variable for every 0 ≤ t ≤ 1
