Flow Matching [14] and Stochastic Interpolants [1]. The framework that we present is most closely related to the frameworks of flow matching and stochastic interpolants (SIs). As we learnt, flow matching restricts itself to flows. In fact, one of the key innovations of flow matching was to show that one does not need a construction via a forward process and SDEs but flow models alone can be trained in a scalable manner. Due to this restriction, you should keep in mind that sampling from a flow matching model will be deterministic (only the initial X0 ∼ pinit will be random). Stochastic interpolants included both the pure flow and the SDE extension via "Langevin dynamics" that we use here (see theorem 13). Stochastic interpolants get their name from a interpolant function I(t, x, z) intended to interpolate between two distributions. In the terminology we use here, this corresponds to a different
